3. R & Shiny Architecture, Frameworks & Best Practices
shinyreact Framework
 * Concept: Shiny UI infrastructure for React-based component rendering while keeping the Shiny server responsible for reactive data computation.
 * Key Architecture & Benefits:
   * While offloading UI rendering to React may feel counterintuitive for traditional Shiny workflows, the major benefits extend far beyond cosmetic improvements.
   * Ecosystem Access: React grants access to a massive ecosystem of sophisticated UI components (e.g., from npm).
   * Granular Control & State: Provides significantly greater control over complex interactions, state management, and reusable components.
   * Enterprise Integration: Simplifies embedding custom Shiny components into complex workflows and enterprise web applications.
Shiny App Architecture & Refactoring Signals
 * Slide Title: Your app might be rootbound if...
 * Signs your app needs refactoring:
   * app.R exceeds 1,000 lines
   * You keep adding sidebar tabs endlessly
   * You have duplicated code blocks
   * Debugging has become noticeably difficult
Shiny Development & Modular Scale (Boehringer Ingelheim)
 * Core Metrics: 20 modules • 120 apps • 20,000 monthly visits
 * What Makes Modularity Work at Scale:
   * Quality: Modules follow best coding practices and validation concepts.
   * Sustainability: Shared modules reduce maintenance work and avoid unsupported custom solutions.
   * Efficiency: Teams save time by using pre-built building blocks.
   * Consistency: A unified look and feel improves usability and user acceptance.
   * Flexibility: Modular design allows trial-specific adaptations while keeping standards.
 * Key Learnings:
   * Focus on reuse potential: Not every feature belongs in the framework. Repeated custom solutions could indicate a missing module. Direct exchange with app creators is essential to uncover reuse potential.
   * Standardize interfaces early: Consistent interfaces make modules easier to set up. Retrofitting standards becomes difficult as the framework grows.
